謝謝 Huli 的批改 🦊

## Config Serializers 
I've revamped the entire config and the way it functions. The saving and loading processes are now dependent on the Google Gson serializers and deserializers. It's easier to register the config categories & sub-categories but most importantly settings/options!

## How it works?
Here's an example of how to register a group of settings:
(Take in mind, all groups are meant to be registered in `ConfigManager.java`)
```java
@Override
public void initialize() {
    // Initial settings and creation of memory placements
    this.register(new SoundsGroup("sounds"));
    
    //...
}
```
Sub-categories, however, are meant to be registered inside of a group class.
Don't worry! Everything has been already moved to work with this brand new system.
```java
this.register(new AutomationGroup("automation"));
this.register(new CommandsGroup("commands"));
this.register(new HidingGroup("hiding"));
this.register(new KeybindsGroup("keybinds"));
this.register(new HighlightGroup("highlight"));
this.register(new ScreenGroup("screen"));
this.register(new MiscellaneousGroup("misc"));
```
## How to I access an option?
For getting a setting value you're going to need: ```CodeUtilsConfig.java```.
It's nothing hard! Here's an example of obtaining a boolean value:
```java
// We're using the class mentioned above. Remember to provide a valid key path!
 if (CodeUtilsConfig.getBoolean("stackDuplicateMsgs")) {
       // some code...
 }
```

## Final Note
The config now only saves when you quit the game, and it loads when the mod is being loaded.
During your game, all settings are kept in the mod's memory to provide the fastest solution to access them in code.
I've done a lot of testing and I think everything should work fine. I recommend some more testing though :)

